# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
*.prof

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Go
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# go.work is committed deliberately (see ADR-0004): it is a developer-experience
# convenience only. CI builds with GOWORK=off so that inter-module coupling is
# always proven against published module versions, never against local paths.
go.work.sum
vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .context — only versioned classifications are tracked (see ADR-0006)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.context/plans/
.context/cache/
.context/runtime/
.context/**/archive/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated AI-tool exports
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .claude/ is a generated export of .context/ for Claude Code, and is NOT
# versioned (ADR-0019, superseding ADR-0017). The exporter re-adds its built-in
# skills, so the tree carries ten skills .context/ never had — three of them
# pruned by name with recorded reasons. One reviewed roster, and it lives in
# .context/.
#
# `make doctor` reports when the export is missing.
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Property-test failure artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# rapid writes testdata/rapid/*.fail so a found counterexample replays. Useful
# while debugging, wrong to commit: most of ours come from deliberately breaking
# a codec to prove the test can go red, and that debris is meaningless later.
#
# A genuine regression becomes a written test case with a name and a reason —
# not an opaque seed file.
**/testdata/rapid/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling / editor state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JetBrains project files mix shared configuration with machine-local paths and
# per-user state in the same files. Committing them produces constant noise and
# occasional breakage; .editorconfig covers what actually needs sharing.
.idea/

# VS Code: share only what makes the repository's own rules easy to satisfy
# (ADR-0016). Personal preferences stay in user settings.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/README.md
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — defence in depth; gitleaks is the enforcing mechanism (M3)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# dotcontext runtime state
.context/cache/semantic/

